1.8: the cattn:q_proj bimodality is the compressor emits on g_side, the "free 4.4 ms" does not exist, and the fork it exposed is worth a paired 0.81 ms/forward

WHAT WAS ASKED. 0.4 left one open lead: at fixed verify width, fixed shape and fixed context,
`q:wq_a` ran 1.71 ms on some verify steps and 5.47 on others -- a 3.2x swing in one fp8 GEMM, with
`cattn:compress` splitting the same way. `cattn:q_proj` is 14.6 ms of every step, so 0.4 recorded
that "if the cheap mode is reachable on demand that is ~4.4 ms/step of Term A for free".

WHAT IT IS. `compressed_verify_step_indexer` records `g_side_fork` and then issues `build_qKV` on
the MAIN stream, so the two `compressor_emit_group` calls run concurrently with the q chain
(F55/F56). The emits fire only for groups completing inside the block -- `(j+1)%ratio==0` -- and the
dprof marks are CUDA events on the main stream, so on an emit step they time a GEMM sharing the
memory system with 21 layers x 2 compressor emits, and on a non-emit step they time it alone.

MEASURED, IN THREE INDEPENDENT WAYS.

1. THE SCHEDULE, AT ZERO GPU COST. `g = #{ j in [ctx,ctx+VB) : (j+1)%4 == 0 }` comes straight out of
   the dprof tag. It classifies 0.4's OWN 153 per-verify tables 153/153, gap 2.80x, no overlap
   between the populations -- on data collected before the hypothesis existed. The excess is LINEAR
   in g: q_proj+compress is +6.97 ms at g=1 and +14.78 at g=2.

2. THE CAUSE, TWO ARMS, ONE BINARY, SERIAL FIRST SO DRIFT PENALISES THE SHIPPED ARM. Four
   predictions registered in scripts/qproj_ab_run.sh before it ran; all four held. At VB=2 held
   fixed (g correlates with width by construction):

     arm     g   q:wq_a   cattn:q_proj   cattn:compress   sum
     serial  0     1.65        10.11            0.05     10.16
     serial  1     1.66        10.12            8.34     18.46
     split   0     1.66        10.12            0.04     10.16
     split   1     5.54        14.68            2.50     17.18

   The swing exists only when the fork does: 1.00-1.02x serial, 3.05x split (174/174 separated).
   The g=0 baseline is 10.16 ms in BOTH arms across two separate checkpoint loads.

3. THE TAIL, UNPLANNED. Every cattn:compress sample above 20 ms -- 8 of 8 across both arms, 43-50 ms
   each, plus the lone outlier in 0.4's table -- is a block containing a RATIO-128 boundary, i.e.
   the 20 strided layers, which use no side stream at all.

THE RATCHET. Paired per leg, same corpus sha: 9 of 9 legs faster under the fork, mean -0.81
ms/forward, sd 0.14, 2 SE band [-0.90, -0.72]; 9/9 byte-identical, tau and realised width equal to
three decimals on every leg. The mark-level instrument predicts that band from the other side:
1.29 ms hidden per emit step x 113/174 emit steps = 0.838 ms/forward, inside it.

WHAT IT MEANS. There is no cheap mode; there is the absence of an emit. Overlap hides 16-17 % of the
compressor and the other 84 % is work a correct engine must do, so `a` stays 125.11 ms and 4.4 ms of
phantom headroom leaves this ladder before an iteration was spent chasing it. What the item bought
instead is the first price on the compressed-KV emit: 7.02 ms on the 64.9 % of forwards that carry
one = 4.56 ms/forward amortised, 3.3 % of the forward, at 52 % of its 880 MB byte roofline.

BIT-EXACTNESS. Nothing numeric changed in either arm -- NO_ATTN_SPLIT only moves kernels between
streams and the fork/join keeps the dependency order identical -- and 9/9 legs proved it.

NEW ON THE LADDER, with pre-registered and honestly small ceilings: 1.11 defer the ATTN_SPLIT join
past i:qidx/i:iw (1.99 ms of independent main-stream work is on the wrong side of it; ceiling
1.29 ms/forward, and this item does NOT establish it is recoverable); 1.12 the ratio-128 emit
re-reads its 33.55 MB of f32 weights ceil(256/8)=32 times (43-50 ms in a single step, ~0.53
ms/forward amortised).

RULE 5 IS ONE ITERATION FROM FIRING. 1.7 shipped a kernel, 1.8 did not. The next iteration takes a
kernel item.

WIKI, same commit: measurement-and-traps.md §29 (a mark that timed another stream's work),
negative-results.md §4h (headroom that was never there), kernel-optimisations.md §2.4b (the
compressor fork, re-measured with a band), README.md state table gains an "after 1.8" column.

Instruments: tools/qproj_bimodal.py (schedule classifier, runs on any dprof server log);
scripts/qproj_ab_run.sh (both arms, detached, added to detach_audit.sh PATTERNS in this commit).
